assistant: Subject: Convert cents to dollars for vendor API 2026-10-01

From vendor API version 2026-10-01 on, `/products` sends `price` in cents (119900) where it used to send dollars (1199). The spec still just says "Unit price", so it gives no hint of the change. `search_products` copied `price` straight through, so it returned prices 100× too high. The fix in `src/tools/search_products.ts` reads the `vendor-api-version` response header and divides prices by 100 when the version is 2026-10-01 or later. Older versions pass through unchanged, so the v1 fixtures give exactly the same output. Typecheck, lint and all tests pass, including the repro test. `get_product` passes `price` through the same way and probably has the same bug on v2. I didn't change it because there's no failing recording for it.

